cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DecaScan in academic or technical work, please cite it as below."
title: "DecaScan: a scanner for the OWASP MCP, LLM applications and web Top 10 lists"
abstract: >-
  DecaScan is a static scanner that checks source code against three
  OWASP Top 10 lists: the MCP Top 10, the Top 10 for LLM Applications 2025, and
  the web Top 10 2021. It reads manifests, configuration and Python and
  TypeScript/JavaScript source, detects which lists apply to a project, and
  reports findings grouped by list and category as terminal output, JSON, SARIF
  or GitHub annotations. It makes no network calls and needs no API key.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Srinivas
    family-names: Chippagiri
repository-code: "https://github.com/cvas22/decascan"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - OWASP
  - OWASP Top 10
  - MCP
  - Model Context Protocol
  - LLM security
  - static analysis
  - SARIF
  - supply chain
